    "historicalContext": "Cadillac arrived at Sepang with the cleaner operating window it found in Baku, but a high-speed circuit, 58°C track temperatures and a rough surface exposed the MAC-26's remaining tyre-management and outright-pace deficit. Bottas described a smooth, issue-free weekend and both drivers were more comfortable with the balance, so the Q1 P21/P22 result is a circuit-fit limitation rather than a disrupted qualifying; the team also chose to save Pérez's new engine for a more favourable venue. Grid penalties for Colapinto and Lindblad lift Bottas and Pérez to P19 and P20 for the start.",
    "driverNotes": {
      "PER": {
        "headline": "Perez finished P19 after Cadillac's slick-tyre gamble immediately gave way to intermediates, then a seven-stop race repeatedly had its recovery neutralised by Safety Cars; the team nevertheless completed all 55 laps and gathered its first competitive wet-weather data.",
        "tag": "seven-stops-wet-weather-learning"
      },
      "BOT": {
        "headline": "Bottas's soft-slick start was untenable on Sepang's wet surface: chasing the intermediate-shod pack, he lost the rear at Turn 13 on lap 9 and beached the MAC-26 in the gravel, triggering the first Safety Car.",
        "tag": "lap-9-turn-13-wet-spin"
      }
    }
